{
  "_note": "labelled fixtures for the lookup. written by the same hand as the tables, so a pass proves the code agrees with the table rather than that the table is right. the contrast pairs are the cases that matter: two numbers from the same market that must not get the same answer.",
  "_contract": "a case names what the plan must be able to say. expected_unknown marks the answers that must stay unknown: claiming more is overreach and the runner counts it separately.",
